Open the next window with an app ID on a workspace asked for it

niri opens a new window on a workspace of its choosing only by a window
rule naming a named workspace, so a program starting a window for a
place known only as it starts, as the shell does a session another
session started, had it open on the focused workspace and moved it
after: it flashed on Joel's screen and its column took his place.

A new action, OpenNextWindowOn { app_id, reference }, says the next
window with that app ID opens on that workspace. The window is placed
there at its initial configure, before every window rule, sized for it,
and added to it on map, without the focus moving; the expectation is
used once, a later one for the same app ID replaces it, and it's
forgotten after 30 seconds or when its workspace goes.

